(Regression test: `write` must interpolate format strings. The parser
 read write's value as a raw StringLit without the format-string check
 that print/copy/append had - all such checks now go through one
 string_value_expr helper - so `write "{x}" to f` shipped writing the
 braces literally.)

a text called name is "world".
a number called n is 42.

Open a file at 1 for writing called out.
write "write: hello {name} {n}\n" to out.
write "write hex: {n:04x}\n" to out.

(write a format string to a real file, read it back)
a text called path is "/tmp/vox_test_write_fmt.txt".
Open a file at path for writing called f.
write "file: {name}-{n}\n" to f.
close f.

Create a buffer called readback.
Open a file at path for reading called f2.
read from f2 into readback.
close f2.
Print readback without newline.
Delete the file path.
